                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "NCqtX",
                      "name": "Body",
                      "fill": "$text-muted-dark",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "[data-theme='dark'] redefines --positive and neither --danger nor --warning. The backoffice is dark by default and ships .tag--danger { color: var(--danger) }, so B3261E is painted on 201D1B at 2.56:1 — under WCAG AA's 4.5:1 for body text. Both proposals keep the hue and saturation of their light sibling and lift only lightness, which is the move the dark theme already makes for --positive and --accent. Both values are declared in design/mockups/proposals.json with their measured ratio.",
